mlg_lib NEWS

* Version 2.0

** Incompatible changes

- The C extension library, libmlg, has been removed, and is no longer
  built or installed.  Every procedure it provided is now written in
  Scheme (wcwidth, string-crc16, real->integer, send-alist-to-journal
  and send-alist-to-syslog) or called through Guile's FFI
  (getpagesize).  Building the package no longer needs a C compiler,
  libtool, gettext, or the systemd development headers.

- characters-load-extension and math-load-extension now do nothing.
  They are kept so that existing callers keep working.

- (mlg utils) no longer exports utils-extensions, which was never
  defined.

- isprint? and ascii-isprint? in (mlg characters), and isprint? and
  ispunct? in (ryu core), now follow C: isprint? is graphic characters
  and space, without tabs or newlines, and ispunct? includes symbols
  such as $, + and ~.

- send-alist-to-journal and send-alist-to-syslog return 0 and #f when
  the journal or syslog daemon cannot be reached, instead of reporting
  success.

- log-error, and other fatal log messages, enter the debugging REPL
  before exiting when the program is interactive and breakpoints are
  enabled with (mlg debug).  Non-interactive programs exit with status
  1, as before.

- In (ryu core), strtol, strtoimax and related procedures clamp
  out-of-range values to the C limits, ctolower and ctoupper return
  their argument unchanged when there is no case mapping, and
  snprintf keeps N - 1 characters, as in C.

- In (ryu printf), %n takes a procedure, which is called with the
  number of characters output so far.  Integer conversions raise an
  error for values outside the range of their C type.

** New features

- (mlg characters) exports wcwidth.  It gives the same results as
  glibc's wcwidth in a UTF-8 locale for every code point, whatever the
  current locale.

- (mlg journal) exports the parameters journal-socket-path and
  syslog-socket-path.

- (mlg regex) is now built and installed.

- (mlg math) array-sum-product-of-slice-pairs, which was exported but
  undefined, is now implemented.

- (ryu core) adds strtoul, strtoumax, nextafter, strncat, strnlen,
  strtok, memmove and other procedures that were exported but
  undefined, and implements the math procedures that were stubs:
  ilogb, logb, ldexp, scalbn, log2, modf, cbrt, hypot, erf, tgamma,
  lgamma, lround, fmod, remquo and fdim.

** Bug fixes

- (ryu printf) now matches glibc's printf for every flag, width,
  precision and conversion, including %g, %a, the h length modifier,
  and .* precisions.

- (mlg logging) prints the level name (WARNING, DEBUG and so on),
  reports 1-based line numbers from the call site, and recovers when a
  log writer raises an error.

- assert evaluates its expression only once and reports 1-based line
  numbers.

- string-crc16, real->integer and getpagesize were exported but
  unbound, because their extensions were never loaded.  They now work.

- read-bytevector, bytevector-u8-map-to-list and string-cell-length
  were quadratic, and are now linear.

- Many smaller fixes in (mlg characters), (mlg math), (mlg port),
  (mlg strings), (mlg time), (mlg utils) and (ryu core).  See the git
  log for details.

* Version 1.0

Initial release.
